":"MASK","links":null}],"title":"Mask Preview","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"MaskPreview"}},{"id":12,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[548,682],"size":[1076,136],"flags":{},"order":2,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Mask nodes","properties":{},"widgets_values":["## Mask nodes\n\n- **Grow Mask:** MASK → bigger MASK. A little extra room blends the edges.\n- **Mask Preview:** shows the mask as black/white - great for debugging."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## Mask nodes\n\n- **Grow Mask:** MASK → bigger MASK. A little extra room blends the edges.\n- **Mask Preview:** shows the mask as black/white - great for debugging."},"color":"#232","bgcolor":"#353"},{"id":13,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[1910,1004],"size":[806,155],"flags":{},"order":3,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Inpaint Model Conditioning","properties":{},"widgets_values":["## Inpaint Model Conditioning\n\nTakes positive, negative, VAE, the image and the mask → outputs **three** things: positive, negative **and** LATENT. All three go into the KSampler.\n**noise_mask = true** keeps sampling inside the mask."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## Inpaint Model Conditioning\n\nTakes positive, negative, VAE, the image and the mask → outputs **three** things: positive, negative **and** LATENT. All three go into the KSampler.\n**noise_mask = true** keeps sampling inside the mask."},"color":"#232","bgcolor":"#353"},{"id":14,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[3426,1304],"size":[1040,174],"flags":{},"order":4,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Composite + Try this","properties":{},"widgets_values":["## Composite + Try this\n\n**ImageCompositeMasked** pastes the new pixels back into the original **only inside the mask**, so the rest stays 100% untouched.\n\n**Try this:** change the prompt to *a knocked-over medical cart with spilled vials* / *a pool of dried blood and a torn crew patch*. Then load `medbay_day.png`, mask the **bed**, and make it *an open cryo pod leaking frost* - a quick way to make story variants of a room."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## Composite + Try this\n\n**ImageCompositeMasked** pastes the new pixels back into the original **only inside the mask**, so the rest stays 100% untouched.\n\n**Try this:** change the prompt to *a knocked-over medical cart with spilled vials* / *a pool of dried blood and a torn crew patch*. Then load `medbay_day.png`, mask the **bed**, and make it *an open cryo pod leaking frost* - a quick way to make story variants of a room."},"color":"#232","bgcolor":"#353"},{"id":15,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[-640,40],"size":[560,554],"flags":{},"order":5,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"08 · Inpainting: change only part of an image","properties":{},"widgets_values":["## 08 · Inpainting: change only part of an image\n\nPaint a **mask** (white = change this) and only that area is regenerated.\n\nThe sample (your Meridian **medbay**) already has a mask on the empty floor right of the bed. **To paint your own:** right-click the Load Image node → **Open in MaskEditor**, paint over the area, **Save**. (The mask is stored in the image's transparency.)\n\nLoad Image has **two outputs**: IMAGE and **MASK**.\n\n### How to use every tutorial\n1. Read this box, then the boxes **below** the nodes (left → right).\n2. Click **Run** (or **Ctrl+Enter**). The result appears in the Save/Preview node and the queue panel.\n3. Do the **Try this** experiments and Run again - learning = changing one thing at a time.\n\n**Reading the graph:** coloured frames run **left → right**: 1 MODELS → 2 INPUTS → 3 PROMPTS → 4 GENERATE → 5 OUTPUT. Wires only turn in the gaps between columns; the **dots** on wires are *reroutes* (drag one to re-route a wire). Follow a wire by its colour = its data type.\n\n**Canvas tips:** drag empty space to pan · scroll to zoom · **.** fits everything · double-click empty canvas to **search & add a node** · click a node + **Ctrl+B** bypasses it · **Ctrl+Z** undo."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"## 08 · Inpainting: change only part of an image\n\nPaint a **mask** (white = change this) and only that area is regenerated.\n\nThe sample (your Meridian **medbay**) already has a mask on the empty floor right of the bed. **To paint your own:** right-click the Load Image node → **Open in MaskEditor**, paint over the area, **Save**. (The mask is stored in the image's transparency.)\n\nLoad Image has **two outputs**: IMAGE and **MASK**.\n\n### How to use every tutorial\n1. Read this box, then the boxes **below** the nodes (left → right).\n2. Click **Run** (or **Ctrl+Enter**). The result appears in the Save/Preview node and the queue panel.\n3. Do the **Try this** experiments and Run again - learning = changing one thing at a time.\n\n**Reading the graph:** coloured frames run **left → right**: 1 MODELS → 2 INPUTS → 3 PROMPTS → 4 GENERATE → 5 OUTPUT. Wires only turn in the gaps between columns; the **dots** on wires are *reroutes* (drag one to re-route a wire). Follow a wire by its colour = its data type.\n\n**Canvas tips:** drag empty space to pan · scroll to zoom · **.** fits everything · double-click empty canvas to **search & add a node** · click a node + **Ctrl+B** bypasses it · **Ctrl+Z** undo."},"color":"#223","bgcolor":"#335"}],"links":[[20,2,1,3,0,"MASK"],[21,1,1,4,0,"CLIP"],[22,1,1,5,0,"CLIP"],[23,4,0,6,0,"CONDITIONING"],[24,5,0,6,1,"CONDITIONING"],[25,1,2,6,2,"VAE"],[26,2,0,6,3,"IMAGE"],[27,3,0,6,4,"MASK"],[28,1,0,7,0,"MODEL"],[29,6,0,7,1,"CONDITIONING"],[30,6,1,7,2,"CONDITIONING"],[31,6,2,7,3,"LATENT"],[32,7,0,8,0,"LATENT"],[33,1,2,8,1,"VAE"],[34,2,0,9,0,"IMAGE"],[35,8,0,9,1,"IMAGE"],[36,3,0,9,2,"MASK"],[37,9,0,10,0,"IMAGE"],[38,3,0,11,0,"MASK"]],"groups":[{"id":1,"title":"1 · MODELS","bounding":[0,0,368,300],"color":"#A88","flags":{}},{"id":2,"title":"2 · INPUTS","bounding":[514,0,1144,882],"color":"#b58b2a","flags":{}},{"id":3,"title":"3 · PROMPTS & CONDITIONING","bounding":[1876,0,874,1223],"color":"#88A","flags":{}},{"id":4,"title":"4 · GENERATE","bounding":[